# The owner's public SSH signing key, in git's allowed-signers format (ssh-keygen(1)
# ALLOWED SIGNERS). Hal's updater checks every new commit against the copy of this file in the version
# already installed, so a push can never bring its own key.
#
# No key is here yet: the owner has not set up commit signing. Until a key line is added, updates install
# without the check, and Settings, Updates says so. To switch the check on, see
# docs/dev/release-and-update.md, "Signing your commits". A key line looks like:
#
#   you@example.invalid namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAA...
